<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil firm, meal firm.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil firm, meal firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in the markets of central India on Tuesday, dealers said. Demand from processing plants was good. Business volume was good and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on limited supplies against good demand in local markets. Soyoil solvent was up by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was up by 300 rupees per tonne. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on good export enquiries but trading activity was dull. Soymeal yellow was $274-276 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) at west Indian ports. Rapeseed extraction was $103-105 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for exports and was 3,450-3,500 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
